.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAP-REBALANCE-APPLICATION 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eap-rebalance-application \- spread an application's instances over the worker nodes again
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eap rebalance-application
\fB\-\-application\-id\fR \fIname\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Asks the manager to move an application's instances to where placement
would put them today:
.IP \(bu 3
onto a node that has joined since they were placed,
.IP \(bu 3
off a node that holds more than its share for the cores it has,
.IP \(bu 3
off a node that is drained, no longer live, or no longer matches the
application's node labels.
.PP
The manager does this by itself after an instance goes away (scaled
down, stopped, taken off a node). This command is for every other time:
a new node, or a pool that ended up lopsided and has not been scaled
since.
.PP
The manager moves one instance per pass. Each move stops one instance
and starts its replacement on the better node on the next pass, so the
pool is at most one instance short while a move is under way, and only
once all its instances are running. Moves continue until no move would
help; an application that is already balanced is left exactly as it is.
Nothing else is restarted.
.PP
It applies even when
.I euclid.modules.eap.rebalance
is
.IR false ,
which turns off only the automatic kind.
.PP
The command returns as soon as the request is recorded.
.BR euclid-cli-emm-list-modules (1)
shows where the instances are as they move, and the manager's log has
"Rebalancing a node application" for each move and "Rebalance done"
at the end.
.PP
A
.I JOB
is refused: moving one of its runs would start that run again. The
caller must be an administrator.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-application\-id " " \fIname\fR
The application to rebalance, in the caller's account and namespace.
.SH OUTPUT
The JSON response has
.IR applicationId ,
.I rebalancing
.RI ( true )
and
.IR instances ,
the number of instances the application has now.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eap rebalance-application --application-id file-pickup
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
